# tools/mycelium_tenure_knot_witness.rish — the Tenure reads across a Knot (r3).
#
# Season D (Kresfa & Mycelium) · Mycelium consensus · the contested-name verdict · rung r3.
# Rung 1 resolved a whole Cord Dag into a namespace verdict — who holds each name, whom the agreed
# order turned away. Yet a namespace a family runs for years does not carry its whole past unbroken:
# the Knot ties off a committed prefix into a sealed FoldState so a bounded Dag runs forever, and new
# facts continue onto that seal. This rung makes the Tenure's corpus a Knot plus its live suffix.
#
# The crux this witness proves: a name won inside a sealed checkpoint stays held when new facts
# continue the log — the holder is the SAME keeper whether the winning reservation lives in a full Cord
# or a sealed Knot, and a later contestant loses that name across the cut exactly as within one
# unbroken resolution (a lawful no-op). The integrity gate holds across the cut three ways: a corrupt
# Knot refuses before a fact is folded, a tampered suffix fact refuses IdentityRefused, and an
# overdrawing suffix refuses Overdraw against the sealed supply. Composes tenure.rye + cord_knot.rye +
# cord.rye + fold.rye public API only, editing no elder's behavior. Demo keeper seeds only — no real
# key, no funds, no network, no custody.
#
# Scope: active-designing/20260813-060935_mycelium-tenure-contested-name-exploration.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/mycelium_tenure_knot_witness.rish

say "mycelium-tenure-knot: Language EN — a name won inside a sealed checkpoint stays held when new facts continue the log."
say "mycelium-tenure-knot: Style Radiant — the Cord tied off the past into a Knot; the Tenure reads across it and the same keeper still holds the name."
say "mycelium-tenure-knot: Lens TAME — the verdict composes tenure + cord_knot public API; every buffer bounded; a contest across the cut is a lawful no-op, corruption refuses whole; demo seeds only, no key held."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "mycelium/bin/tenure-knot"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/tenure_knot.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "mycelium-tenure-knot: build failed"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "mycelium-tenure-knot: selftest exited non-zero"
assert selftest.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: selftest did not speak GREEN"
assert selftest.out contains "the suffix contests it and loses" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: sealed-winner claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "stays held by the same keeper across the cut" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: holder-never-drifts claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "each refuse whole" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: integrity-across-the-cut claim missing"
assert selftest.out contains "holder never drifts" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: crux GREEN line missing"

# The Tenure whose verdict this rung carries across a checkpoint, and the Knot that ties off the
# committed prefix, both stand at the door — their own selftests prove the machinery r3 rests on.
let tenure = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/tenure.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/tenure && mycelium/bin/tenure 2>&1"]
assert tenure.ok else "mycelium-tenure-knot: the Tenure r1 the checkpoint carries is not GREEN"
assert tenure.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: the Tenure r1 did not speak its GREEN"

let knot = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p mycelium/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build mycelium/cord_knot.rye -femit-bin=mycelium/bin/cord-knot && mycelium/bin/cord-knot 2>&1"]
assert knot.ok else "mycelium-tenure-knot: the Knot the verdict reads across is not GREEN"
assert knot.out contains "GREEN" else "mycelium-tenure-knot: the Knot did not speak its GREEN"

say "mycelium-tenure-knot: GREEN — a name won in a sealed Knot stays held as the suffix contests and loses; the holder never drifts between a full Cord and a checkpoint; a corrupt Knot, a tampered fact, and an overdraw each refuse whole; the Tenure and the Knot stand at the door."
